    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 92,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Publish 1.x built by core** (`make core_publish`): the steps and their owners are on the \"Publish 1.x from core\" card in WEB-startr.style.core/TODO.md"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 93,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "1.4.0 live 2026-10-16 (tag v1.4.0): /style.css b845cff\u2026, /startr.css and /props.json from core; /style-core/ pages styled again"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 94,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "1.4.1 hotfix 2026-10-17 (tag v1.4.1, /style.css 931e22f\u2026): 1.4.0's `button:hover` painted over a consumer's own reset (AI-UI's transparent icon buttons went solid primary); now `:where(button, \u2026):hover`. Found by the regression run; `bun run probe:hover` in core is the gate"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 95,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "1.4.2 hotfix 2026-10-17 (tag v1.4.2, /style.css c10bda2\u2026): 1.4.1 still outranked Tailwind's preflight; each hover selector now carries its base rule's specificity (`button:where(:hover)`); 0 unasked fills on AI-UI's real pages with the core's `probe:hover --sheet` before release"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 96,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Move the /style.min.css consumers to the current min after a visual check** (Sage.is, Startr.cloud): `HOLD_MIN ?= 1.3.2` in the Makefile keeps the drifted 1.3.2 min; the current min changes ~250 element rules for them. Empty HOLD_MIN once checked"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 98,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[MANUALLY] **Narrow the Cloudflare image rule**: a redirect rule on the startr.style zone (not Netlify: no x-nf-request-id) sends dotted first segments to image.startr.cloud, and real files do not shadow it; /v1.3.2/ and /v1.4.0/ 302 (2026-10-16). Match numeric WxH only"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 99,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Ship pinned and rolling CDN versions**: Currently unversioned \u2014 any change to Startr.Style hits every consumer (Sage.is, Sage.Education) instantly, with no rollback path."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 100,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Per-release pins: `make version_snapshot` wrote `/v1.3.2/`, `/v1.4.0/`, `/v1.4.1/`, `/v1.4.2/` under src/static (2026-10-16/17); served once the Cloudflare rule is narrowed"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 101,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Publish `/v1/`, `/v2/`, and a rolling `/latest/`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 102,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Implementation approach: submodule structure where `v1/` is a submodule pointing to the project at the v1 tag, `v2/` at v2, etc. \u2014 versioned URLs serve from the pinned submodule, `latest/` serves from `master`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 103,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Consumers pin to a version in prod; `latest` is for the Startr studio itself. Migration plan needed for existing Sage.is / Sage.Education `<link>` tags currently pointing at the unversioned URL. *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman in a panel review of Sage.is, 2026-04-18.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 104,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Cache headers \u2014 versioned vs rolling** *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman, 2026-04-18.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 105,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/v1/style.css`, `/v2/style.css`, etc. \u2192 `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` (one year, immutable; the URL's contents never change by design): `netlify.toml` gives `/v*/*` that header; `/v1/swap.js` answers it (2026-10-18)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 106,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/latest/style.css` \u2192 `Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, must-revalidate` (short TTL + revalidate so studio pushes propagate quickly and stale copies don't linger)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 107,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Emit SRI integrity hashes for each pinned release**: Generate `sha384` integrity hashes at release time and publish them alongside the versioned URL. *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman, 2026-04-18.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 110,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Resolve version drift between README and package.json**: `README.md` opens with `1.3.2`; `package.json` declares `1.4.2` (2026-10-18). Filed at `1.3.1` vs `1.2.2.2`; the licence card closed it once at 1.3.2."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 111,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Pick one source of truth (conventionally `package.json`) and make the README read from it, or bump them in lockstep via `scripts/release.sh`. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "772b3b1ec9ffab19",
      "line_num": 89,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\ud83d\udce6 Versioning & Rollback**\n- [x] **Publish 1.x built by core** (`make core_publish`): the steps and their owners are on the \"Publish 1.x from core\" card in WEB-startr.style.core/TODO.md\n- [x] 1.4.0 live 2026-10-16 (tag v1.4.0): /style.css b845cff\u2026, /startr.css and /props.json from core; /style-core/ pages styled again\n- [x] 1.4.1 hotfix 2026-10-17 (tag v1.4.1, /style.css 931e22f\u2026): 1.4.0's `button:hover` painted over a consumer's own reset (AI-UI's transparent icon buttons went solid primary); now `:where(button, \u2026):hover`. Found by the regression run; `bun run probe:hover` in core is the gate\n- [x] 1.4.2 hotfix 2026-10-17 (tag v1.4.2, /style.css c10bda2\u2026): 1.4.1 still outranked Tailwind's preflight; each hover selector now carries its base rule's specificity (`button:where(:hover)`); 0 unasked fills on AI-UI's real pages with the core's `probe:hover --sheet` before release\n- [ ] **Move the /style.min.css consumers to the current min after a visual check** (Sage.is, Startr.cloud): `HOLD_MIN ?= 1.3.2` in the Makefile keeps the drifted 1.3.2 min; the current min changes ~250 element rules for them. Empty HOLD_MIN once checked\n- [ ] [MANUALLY] **Narrow the Cloudflare image rule**: a redirect rule on the startr.style zone (not Netlify: no x-nf-request-id) sends dotted first segments to image.startr.cloud, and real files do not shadow it; /v1.3.2/ and /v1.4.0/ 302 (2026-10-16). Match numeric WxH only\n- [ ] **Ship pinned and rolling CDN versions**: Currently unversioned \u2014 any change to Startr.Style hits every consumer (Sage.is, Sage.Education) instantly, with no rollback path.\n- [x] Per-release pins: `make version_snapshot` wrote `/v1.3.2/`, `/v1.4.0/`, `/v1.4.1/`, `/v1.4.2/` under src/static (2026-10-16/17); served once the Cloudflare rule is narrowed\n- [ ] Publish `/v1/`, `/v2/`, and a rolling `/latest/`.\n- [ ] Implementation approach: submodule structure where `v1/` is a submodule pointing to the project at the v1 tag, `v2/` at v2, etc. \u2014 versioned URLs serve from the pinned submodule, `latest/` serves from `master`.\n- [ ] Consumers pin to a version in prod; `latest` is for the Startr studio itself. Migration plan needed for existing Sage.is / Sage.Education `<link>` tags currently pointing at the unversioned URL. *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman in a panel review of Sage.is, 2026-04-18.)*\n- [ ] **Cache headers \u2014 versioned vs rolling** *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman, 2026-04-18.)*\n- [x] `/v1/style.css`, `/v2/style.css`, etc. \u2192 `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` (one year, immutable; the URL's contents never change by design): `netlify.toml` gives `/v*/*` that header; `/v1/swap.js` answers it (2026-10-18)\n- [ ] `/latest/style.css` \u2192 `Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, must-revalidate` (short TTL + revalidate so studio pushes propagate quickly and stale copies don't linger).\n- [ ] **Emit SRI integrity hashes for each pinned release**: Generate `sha384` integrity hashes at release time and publish them alongside the versioned URL. *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman, 2026-04-18.)*\n- [ ] **Resolve version drift between README and package.json**: `README.md` opens with `1.3.2`; `package.json` declares `1.4.2` (2026-10-18). Filed at `1.3.1` vs `1.2.2.2`; the licence card closed it once at 1.3.2.\n- [ ] Pick one source of truth (conventionally `package.json`) and make the README read from it, or bump them in lockstep via `scripts/release.sh`. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n\n`TODO.md:L89`",
