      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 115,
          "tags": [
            "#dx",
            "#landmine"
          ],
          "text": "**Give prop typos a failure mode**: An inline prop with no matching `[style*=\"--X:\"]` rule fails silently \u2014 no error, no fallback, the declaration just sits inert."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 117,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Publish the canonical prop list as a JSON artifact per release (extractable from the built sheet by regexing `[style*=\"--X:\"]` selectors \u2014 proof-of-concept script exists in build.sage.education's `--br` audit)."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 118,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Core's build writes props.json (every prop, tier, state, collision, deprecation); `make core_publish` copies it to src/static/props.json and src/_data/props.json, and src/docs/utilities.njk renders from it (2026-10-16)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 119,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "scripts/snapshot-version.sh pins no props.json, so a pinned sheet has no pinned dictionary"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 120,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Authoring-time linter: check every `--*` in template `style=\"\"` attributes against that list; run in consumer CI."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 121,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Core's `bun run ingest <page>` lints inline props against props.json: unknown, deprecated, collision, tier-state (2026-10-16); consumer CI hookup still open"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 122,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Trellis `make kit_check` lints every template `style=` prop against its vendored props.json and fails on an unknown one (2026-10-16)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 123,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Dev-mode runtime warner: a tiny opt-in script that scans `[style*=\"--\"]` elements and console.warns unknown props."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 124,
          "tags": [
            "#landmine"
          ],
          "text": "**Shorthand dual bindings** (`--br` = border-radius AND border-right; `--bs`, `--td`, `--fs`, `--cr` value-disjoint pairs): the naming decision is filed in `WEB-startr.style.core/TODO.md` \u2014 resolve it there, then mirror the outcome here."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "be1b3c971fcb61a5",
      "line_num": 113,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\ud83e\udde8 Silent-Failure DX \u2014 unknown props are no-ops**\n- [ ] **Give prop typos a failure mode**: An inline prop with no matching `[style*=\"--X:\"]` rule fails silently \u2014 no error, no fallback, the declaration just sits inert. #dx #landmine\n- [x] Publish the canonical prop list as a JSON artifact per release (extractable from the built sheet by regexing `[style*=\"--X:\"]` selectors \u2014 proof-of-concept script exists in build.sage.education's `--br` audit).\n- [x] Core's build writes props.json (every prop, tier, state, collision, deprecation); `make core_publish` copies it to src/static/props.json and src/_data/props.json, and src/docs/utilities.njk renders from it (2026-10-16)\n- [ ] scripts/snapshot-version.sh pins no props.json, so a pinned sheet has no pinned dictionary\n- [ ] Authoring-time linter: check every `--*` in template `style=\"\"` attributes against that list; run in consumer CI.\n- [x] Core's `bun run ingest <page>` lints inline props against props.json: unknown, deprecated, collision, tier-state (2026-10-16); consumer CI hookup still open\n- [x] Trellis `make kit_check` lints every template `style=` prop against its vendored props.json and fails on an unknown one (2026-10-16)\n- [ ] Dev-mode runtime warner: a tiny opt-in script that scans `[style*=\"--\"]` elements and console.warns unknown props.\n- [ ] **Shorthand dual bindings** (`--br` = border-radius AND border-right; `--bs`, `--td`, `--fs`, `--cr` value-disjoint pairs): the naming decision is filed in `WEB-startr.style.core/TODO.md` \u2014 resolve it there, then mirror the outcome here. #landmine\n\n`TODO.md:L113`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 150
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 129,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Audit `-hvr` coverage for `:focus` and `:focus-visible`**: Every `[style*=\"--X-hvr:\"]:hover` rule should be paired with `:focus, :focus-visible` so keyboard users get the same affordance as mouse users. `--shadow-hvr` covers `:focus` today; audit and enumerate the rest (`--hvr-bgc`, `--hvr-c`, `--hvr-bdc`, etc.). Land coverage systematically, not ad-hoc. *(Surfaced by Adam Wathan in a panel review of Sage.is, 2026-04-18.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 130,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Done in core (2026-10-16): every hover rule, the new `--x-hover` props and the `-hvr`/`-hover` helpers, has a `:focus-visible` copy; scripts/bands.test.ts and states.test.ts hold it"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 131,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Reconcile `:focus-visible` audit status with spoken claims**: closed with a landed commit, the `-hvr` coverage audit above (core, 2026-10-16; scripts/bands.test.ts and states.test.ts hold it). *(Surfaced by Heydon Pickering in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "e4d668ae2d4fbe60",
      "line_num": 127,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\u267f Accessibility**\n- [x] **Audit `-hvr` coverage for `:focus` and `:focus-visible`**: Every `[style*=\"--X-hvr:\"]:hover` rule should be paired with `:focus, :focus-visible` so keyboard users get the same affordance as mouse users. `--shadow-hvr` covers `:focus` today; audit and enumerate the rest (`--hvr-bgc`, `--hvr-c`, `--hvr-bdc`, etc.). Land coverage systematically, not ad-hoc. *(Surfaced by Adam Wathan in a panel review of Sage.is, 2026-04-18.)*\n- [x] Done in core (2026-10-16): every hover rule, the new `--x-hover` props and the `-hvr`/`-hover` helpers, has a `:focus-visible` copy; scripts/bands.test.ts and states.test.ts hold it\n- [x] **Reconcile `:focus-visible` audit status with spoken claims**: closed with a landed commit, the `-hvr` coverage audit above (core, 2026-10-16; scripts/bands.test.ts and states.test.ts hold it). *(Surfaced by Heydon Pickering in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n\n`TODO.md:L127`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 240
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 135,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Audit every colour leaf for IACVT-safe fallbacks**: The 216-cell `color-mix(in oklch, \u2026)` cascade in `src/style-core/src/variables.css` invalidates whole declarations when any component is unparseable. Every consumer leaf (e.g. `background: var(--primary)`) must resolve to `var(--primary, <literal-fallback>)`, not `inherit`/`initial`. Audit the whole leaf surface, not one line \u2014 otherwise the DSL has accents. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 136,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Moot since 2026-10-16: the 216-cell cascade is gone (`--mix`/`--tone` compute on the element); the new tints ship literal defaults with color-mix() under @supports"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 137,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Register critical custom properties with `@property`**: Without registration, the browser treats colour and layout variables as untyped strings. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 139,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Register `--primary`, `--background`, `--text-main` so the browser can validate inputs and animate between them; the 216-cell cube entries are moot since 2026-10-16 (the cube is gone)."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 140,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`--mix`, `--tone`, `--tone-of`, `--mixed` and `--toned` are registered, inherits:false (2026-10-16); `--primary`, `--background` and `--text-main` are not"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "74670940d11639a6",
      "line_num": 133,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\ud83c\udfa8 Colour System Invariants**\n- [x] **Audit every colour leaf for IACVT-safe fallbacks**: The 216-cell `color-mix(in oklch, \u2026)` cascade in `src/style-core/src/variables.css` invalidates whole declarations when any component is unparseable. Every consumer leaf (e.g. `background: var(--primary)`) must resolve to `var(--primary, <literal-fallback>)`, not `inherit`/`initial`. Audit the whole leaf surface, not one line \u2014 otherwise the DSL has accents. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n- [x] Moot since 2026-10-16: the 216-cell cascade is gone (`--mix`/`--tone` compute on the element); the new tints ship literal defaults with color-mix() under @supports\n- [ ] **Register critical custom properties with `@property`**: Without registration, the browser treats colour and layout variables as untyped strings. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n- [ ] Register `--primary`, `--background`, `--text-main` so the browser can validate inputs and animate between them; the 216-cell cube entries are moot since 2026-10-16 (the cube is gone).\n- [x] `--mix`, `--tone`, `--tone-of`, `--mixed` and `--toned` are registered, inherits:false (2026-10-16); `--primary`, `--background` and `--text-main` are not\n\n`TODO.md:L133`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 330
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 144,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Replace the \"17% faster than Tailwind\" eye-balling with a real harness**: Pick three comparable pages per site (landing, docs, gallery/component showcase). Throttle to Slow 4G, mid-tier Android, cold cache, five runs, publish median."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 145,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Publish the harness and raw numbers in `docs/benchmarks/`. Until then, the 17% claim is a vibe, not a metric \u2014 use it at parties, not in the README. *(Surfaced by Jeremy Keith in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 146,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Re-run LCP on a page that exercises the colour cube**: Current LCP of 0.55s has `<p>` as the LCP element, meaning the 216-cell `color-mix()` cascade is not in the critical render path of the tested page. Moot since 2026-10-16: the 216-cell cube is gone (`--mix`/`--tone` compute on the element)."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 147,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Re-measure on `theme-creator.html` and the component gallery once it exists \u2014 pages that actually resolve the cube. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)* Moot since 2026-10-16: the 216-cell cube is gone (`--mix`/`--tone` compute on the element)."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "c95dedebb5a2a281",
      "line_num": 142,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\ud83d\udcca Performance Methodology**\n- [ ] **Replace the \"17% faster than Tailwind\" eye-balling with a real harness**: Pick three comparable pages per site (landing, docs, gallery/component showcase). Throttle to Slow 4G, mid-tier Android, cold cache, five runs, publish median.\n- [ ] Publish the harness and raw numbers in `docs/benchmarks/`. Until then, the 17% claim is a vibe, not a metric \u2014 use it at parties, not in the README. *(Surfaced by Jeremy Keith in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n- [x] **Re-run LCP on a page that exercises the colour cube**: Current LCP of 0.55s has `<p>` as the LCP element, meaning the 216-cell `color-mix()` cascade is not in the critical render path of the tested page. Moot since 2026-10-16: the 216-cell cube is gone (`--mix`/`--tone` compute on the element).\n- [x] Re-measure on `theme-creator.html` and the component gallery once it exists \u2014 pages that actually resolve the cube. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)* Moot since 2026-10-16: the 216-cell cube is gone (`--mix`/`--tone` compute on the element).\n\n`TODO.md:L142`",
