          "line_num": 156,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Reset replaced elements to `display: block`**: Startr.Style ships `img { max-width: 100% }` but never resets `display` or `vertical-align`, so every `<img>` stays `display: inline` and sits on the text baseline. *(Surfaced while debugging the Startr.ca card layout, 2026-07-01.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 160,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Decide whether to fold this into the framework's base reset."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 161,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Gauge blast radius before landing**: a global `img { display: block }` shifts any consumer that *intends* inline images flowed with text (icons mid-sentence, inline logos/badges, emoji-style glyphs)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 162,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Before committing, `grep` the known consumers (`WEB-Sage.is`, `WEB-Sage.Education`, `WEB-startr`, `WEB-AI--Sage-is-AI-UI`) for inline-image usage."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 163,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "If the fallout is real, prefer `vertical-align: middle` alone (kills the descender gap while keeping images inline) over forcing `display: block`."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 166,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Enhanced Design Philosophy Pages** - Added comprehensive practical examples to Brutalism, Modernism, and Experimentalism pages"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 167,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Created Tutorial System** - Built step-by-step tutorials covering basic utilities, responsive layouts, and interactive components"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 168,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Added Use Cases Documentation** - Created practical real-world examples including login forms, navigation, galleries, and pricing cards"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 169,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Updated Navigation** - Added Learning section with links to Tutorials and Use Cases, plus Design Styles section"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 170,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Component Inventory Complete** - Scanned existing components and updated TODO with 15+ existing components ready for gallery inclusion"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "b64d1e3874c73fb7",
      "line_num": 154,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f Element Resets**\n- [ ] **Reset replaced elements to `display: block`**: Startr.Style ships `img { max-width: 100% }` but never resets `display` or `vertical-align`, so every `<img>` stays `display: inline` and sits on the text baseline. *(Surfaced while debugging the Startr.ca card layout, 2026-07-01.)*\n- [ ] Decide whether to fold this into the framework's base reset.\n- [ ] **Gauge blast radius before landing**: a global `img { display: block }` shifts any consumer that *intends* inline images flowed with text (icons mid-sentence, inline logos/badges, emoji-style glyphs).\n- [ ] Before committing, `grep` the known consumers (`WEB-Sage.is`, `WEB-Sage.Education`, `WEB-startr`, `WEB-AI--Sage-is-AI-UI`) for inline-image usage.\n- [ ] If the fallout is real, prefer `vertical-align: middle` alone (kills the descender gap while keeping images inline) over forcing `display: block`.\n- [x] **Enhanced Design Philosophy Pages** - Added comprehensive practical examples to Brutalism, Modernism, and Experimentalism pages\n- [x] **Created Tutorial System** - Built step-by-step tutorials covering basic utilities, responsive layouts, and interactive components\n- [x] **Added Use Cases Documentation** - Created practical real-world examples including login forms, navigation, galleries, and pricing cards\n- [x] **Updated Navigation** - Added Learning section with links to Tutorials and Use Cases, plus Design Styles section\n- [x] **Component Inventory Complete** - Scanned existing components and updated TODO with 15+ existing components ready for gallery inclusion\n\n`TODO.md:L154`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 600
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 500,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Either (a) extend the framework's bindings with the form-control selector list, or (b) document the gotcha prominently."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "c5116583da5aa1d7",
      "line_num": 498,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Framework `--c` / `--bg` / `--b` bindings should cover form controls + links: `[style*=\"--c\"] { color: var(--c) }` loses to UA defaults on `<input>`, `<button>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`, `<a>` (system color keywords `ButtonText`/`FieldText` and `-webkit-link` win).**\n- [ ] Either (a) extend the framework's bindings with the form-control selector list, or (b) document the gotcha prominently.\n\n`TODO.md:L498`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 690
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 508,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(a) Document the default behavior + the opt-out in startr.style docs alongside the framework primitives."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 509,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(b) Ship a utility class \u2014 e.g. `.text-flat` or `.no-gradient-text` \u2014 that bundles the three-property opt-out so consumers can write `<button class=\"text-flat\">` instead of remembering the recipe."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 510,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Smarter-defaults option to weigh:** drop `button, .button` from the selector list entirely \u2014 interactive controls almost always have a solid background that hides the gradient anyway."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "9ac848a7e11ab2ee",
      "line_num": 504,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Document the brand \"gradient text\" default + ship `.text-flat` opt-out utility: the site-wide gradient rule leaves invisible text on custom components with solid backgrounds.**\n- [ ] (a) Document the default behavior + the opt-out in startr.style docs alongside the framework primitives.\n- [ ] (b) Ship a utility class \u2014 e.g. `.text-flat` or `.no-gradient-text` \u2014 that bundles the three-property opt-out so consumers can write `<button class=\"text-flat\">` instead of remembering the recipe.\n- [ ] **Smarter-defaults option to weigh:** drop `button, .button` from the selector list entirely \u2014 interactive controls almost always have a solid background that hides the gradient anyway.\n\n`TODO.md:L504`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 780
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "e1cf6ddc3add24dc",
      "line_num": 515,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Typography prop names silently collide with non-typography intents #critical \u2014 Three pairs of identical custom-prop names mean reasonable-looking inline styles silently render as invalid declarations the browser drops without warning:**\n`TODO.md:L515`",
